The study room
==============

Three walls and a floor around a sphere, two boxes, and the Utah teapot, lit by a ceiling panel and the sky; and
the same room standing on wide grounds. The lab reads each scene as the TOML document of its binding
(lab/src/script/data.rs; `render-lab lamlet toml study-room.lam studyRoom` prints it): the resource
`scene/study-room` is `studyRoom`, `scene/study-room-grounds` is `studyRoomGrounds` (lab/src/scene.rs reads them;
scenes/terrain.toml is a scene written as TOML).

Right-handed, +Y up, metres. A rotation is one turn about `x`, `y`, or `z` in degrees, or `aim`: the object's local
+Y turned toward that point.

$[Import* std]

$[# Rotation [% {Variant {'
    {Field "x" Float}
    {Field "y" Float}
    {Field "z" Float}
    {Field "aim" {List Float}}}}]]
$[# Vec [% {List Float}]]

An object: its name and shape (plane, box, sphere, panel, mesh, or terrain), its half extent (a mesh's and the
terrain's are their own), where it stands and how it is turned and scaled, its surface, and its light. The parts
an object leaves out are `none`.

$[# Object [% {Struct {'
    {Field "name" String}
    {Field "shape" String}
    {Field "mesh" {Option String}}
    {Field "extent" {Option Vec}}
    {Field "translation" {Option Vec}}
    {Field "rotation" {Option Rotation}}
    {Field "albedo" Vec}
    {Field "roughness" Float}
    {Field "emissive" {Option Vec}}
    {Field "emissiveStrength" {Option Float}}}}]]
$[# {_object name shape extent albedo roughness} {: {.
    name name
    shape shape
    mesh none
    extent {some extent}
    translation none
    rotation none
    albedo albedo
    roughness roughness
    emissive none
    emissiveStrength none} Object}]
$[# {_at translation o} {.translation= o {some translation}}]
$[# {_turned rotation o} {.rotation= o {some {: rotation Rotation}}}]

The room's walls, from its half width and its height: each a plane through the room's edge, turned to face in.

$[# _half 3.0]
$[# _height 3.0]
$[# {_wall name extent translation rotation albedo} {_turned rotation {_at translation {_object name "plane" extent albedo
    1.0}}}]
$[# _walls [% {'
    {_wall "back wall"
        {' _half 0.0 {/ _height 2.0}}
        {' 0.0 {/ _height 2.0} {neg _half}}
        {#x 90.0}
        {' 0.72 0.70 0.66}}
    {_wall "left wall"
        {' {/ _height 2.0} 0.0 _half}
        {' {neg _half} {/ _height 2.0} 0.0}
        {#z -90.0}
        {' 0.70 0.24 0.18}}
    {_wall "right wall"
        {' {/ _height 2.0} 0.0 _half}
        {' _half {/ _height 2.0} 0.0}
        {#z 90.0}
        {' 0.16 0.55 0.50}}}]]

A ceiling light: the panel's local +Y normal turned to face down; the scene's light is its rectangle, colour, and
radiance.

$[# _panel [% {.emissiveStrength=
    {.emissive=
        {_turned
            {#x 180.0}
            {_at
                {' 0.0 2.95 -0.2}
                {_object "emissive panel" "panel" {' 1.2 0.0 0.6} {' 0.8 0.8 0.8} 1.0}}}
        {some {' 1.0 0.88 0.72}}}
    {some 6.0}}]]

The objects on the floor. The teapot is the bounds demonstration's object: the spout reaches farther than the
handle, so the local bounds' centre is off the pivot. Its bounds are the mesh's.

$[# _objects [% {'
    {_at {' -1.05 0.62 -0.55} {_object "sphere" "sphere" {' 0.62 0.62 0.62} {' 0.86 0.82 0.74} 0.5}}
    {_turned
        {#y 30.0}
        {_at
            {' 1.05 0.45 0.15}
            {_object "rotated box" "box" {' 0.5 0.45 0.38} {' 0.22 0.42 0.85} 0.6}}}
    {_turned
        {#y 20.0}
        {_at
            {' 1.95 0.24 1.45}
            {_object "small box" "box" {' 0.24 0.24 0.24} {' 0.92 0.55 0.22} 0.6}}}
    {_turned
        {#y 30.0}
        {_at
            {' -0.25 0.0 -1.75}
            {.extent=
                {.mesh= {_object "teapot" "mesh" {'} {' 0.50 0.66 0.56} 0.35} {some "teapot"}}
                none}}}}]]

The room: its title (a text key), how far a camera keeps clear (`roomMargin` inside the walls, or `above` the
ground), and its floor's half extent. The objects are in the order of `scene::ids`.

$[# CameraClear [% {Variant {' {Field "roomMargin" Float} {Field "above" Float}}}]]
$[# {_room r} {.
    titleText {.titleText r}
    cameraClear {: {.cameraClear r} CameraClear}
    lighting {.
        light "emissive panel"
        ambient 0.12
        f0 0.04
        reflectionStrength 1.0
        ggxSamples 16
        exposure 1.0}
    object {flatten {'
        {' {_object "floor" "plane" {' {.floor r} 0.0 {.floor r}} {' 0.16 0.17 0.19} 1.0}}
        _walls
        {' _panel}
        _objects}}}]

The study room, seen from inside its walls.

$[# studyRoom [% {_room {.
    titleText "scene.study_room"
    cameraClear {#roomMargin 0.2}
    floor _half}}]]

The study room standing on wide grounds, its floor extended to 600 m a side, for views that pull far out of the
room (cascades of a probe grid, say), seen from above them.

$[# studyRoomGrounds [% {_room {.
    titleText "scene.study_room_grounds"
    cameraClear {#above 0.1}
    floor 300.0}}]]
